message: "If you refer to this article, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Long-Term Memory for AI Characters: Memory, Context and Contextual Emotional Inference in AI Roleplay"
abstract: >-
  An essay on long-term memory for AI characters, written by the founder of
  ChatBrat AI. It argues that useful AI character memory goes beyond storing
  facts: it combines conversational context, history and contextual emotional
  inference (tentative, revisable readings of conversational signals) so that
  remembered history changes how a character behaves. It distinguishes fact
  memory from experience memory, outlines what long-term memory should and
  should not keep, describes an observe-interpret-retrieve-compare-respond-update
  loop, and proposes practical tests for meaningful memory. It is an opinion
  and design essay, not an empirical study, and makes no product-performance
  claims.
